0..56 Comment "// Two nestings of one chain of paths are one composite."
57..59 Comment "//"
60..144 Comment "// A proof then writes `Path.here` where it would cite an associator, and the theory"
145..172 Comment "// adjoins no cell for one."
173..175 Comment "//"
176..250 Comment "// A transport along a stuck composite moves its operand along each of the"
251..330 Comment "// composite\'s paths in turn, in evaluation and in the kernel. Every nesting of"
331..417 Comment "// a chain so reaches the left-nested `Path.step` fold the unbiased composite carries."
418..420 Comment "//"
421..492 Comment "// - see: `compose-chain.gandr` — the unbiased composite and its fold"
493..546 Comment "// - see: `then.gandr` — the composite of two paths"
548..586 Comment "// The circle, its point and its loop."
